= Ecosystem relationship =

BITwiki and BIThub serve different but connected knowledge roles.

== BIThub ==
BIThub is the live forum, workspace, coordination, and discourse layer. Work can begin as discussion, research, guides, artifacts, collaborative reasoning, or workflow output.

== BITwiki ==
BITwiki is the durable MediaWiki knowledge and memory layer. It holds stable pages, references, structured knowledge, hardened definitions, reusable documentation, and long-lived conceptual memory.

== Crystallization ==
Stable, useful signal can move from live work into durable wiki knowledge after review, correction, sourcing, and structuring.

The goal is not to mirror every interaction. The goal is to preserve what is worth reusing.

== Identity and protected memory ==
The wider architecture may connect user identity and protected memory between ecosystem surfaces. Those capabilities require explicit permission boundaries. This public repository represents public wiki content only and contains no protected user material or private operational data.

== Distinctions ==
* A BIThub discussion is not a BITwiki page.
* A Discourse wiki post is still a Discourse post.
* A BITwiki page has MediaWiki revisions, links, categories, namespaces, redirects, talk surfaces, and wiki history.

